# Treat office/document and other binary formats as binary: `git diff` shows
# "Binary files ... differ" instead of a line-by-line dump (this is what made
# vignettes/*.pdf show up as tens of thousands of "+" lines in review diffs).
# To force a real diff when you actually need one:
#   git diff --text -- path/to/file.pdf
#
# Plain text formats (.csv, .txt, .md, .R, .Rmd, .qmd, .yaml, ...) are left
# alone - git already diffs those correctly and quickly.

# Word
*.doc   binary
*.docx  binary
*.dot   binary
*.dotx  binary
*.rtf   binary

# Excel
*.xls   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xlsm  binary
*.xltx  binary

# PowerPoint
*.ppt   binary
*.pptx  binary
*.potx  binary

# PDF
*.pdf   binary

# OpenDocument
*.odt   binary
*.ods   binary
*.odp   binary

# Images / archives / R data
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.gif      binary
*.ico      binary
*.zip      binary
*.rds      binary
*.rda      binary
*.rdata    binary
*.sas7bdat binary
